    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0625" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1468: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Merrell</hi>)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d535-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-10T22:00:00-04:00">December 10,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>701. Gordon Bowles departing immediately for India as representative of B. E.
                        W.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d535-f2"/> and O. L. L. A.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d535-f3"/> to explore motorable routes through Afghanistan and
                    Russian Turkestan with view to opening up new channel for supply of goods to
                    China. Kuibyshev and Kabul have been instructed to request permission of Soviet
                    and Afghan Governments for him and an American mechanic to make the proposed
                    trip through their territories. Please render all appropriate assistance and
                    request cooperation of British and Indian authorities. Repeated to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d535-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d535-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as No. 6757, December 10, 11 p.m., to the Ambassador in the United
                    Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d535-f2" n="3" xml:id="d535-f2-content">
                <p>Board of Economic Warfare.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d535-f3" n="4" xml:id="d535-f3-content">
                <p>Office of Lend-Lease Administration.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
